# Docker build-context exclude list for SairiOS. NOT IN FORCE WHERE IT SITS.
#
# HOW DOCKER RESOLVES THIS FILE
#
# All four Dockerfiles in this directory are built with the REPOSITORY ROOT as
# the build context (`context: ..` in compose.yaml), because npm workspaces
# need the root package.json, the lockfile and every workspace manifest. Docker
# reads `<context>/.dockerignore`, which is the repository root. There is no
# file there, and Docker never reads this one. For the builds documented in
# docs/DOCKER.md, nothing below excludes anything.
#
# What that means in practice: the whole repository is sent to the daemon as
# build context, `.env` and var/ and node_modules/ included. The Dockerfiles do
# not `COPY . .`, so a repository-root `.env` does not reach an image layer,
# but the directory-level copies (`COPY packages/shared ./packages/shared`, and
# the same shape for each built workspace) take whatever sits inside those
# directories: a host node_modules/, a stale dist/, a workspace-local .env or
# key file. This file stops none of that today. Read the list below as a
# statement of intent, not as a control.
#
# TO MAKE IT EFFECTIVE, either:
#
#   1. Put a `.dockerignore` at the repository root. That is the path Docker
#      reads for these builds, and it works on every builder.
#   2. Or add a per-Dockerfile ignore file named
#      `<path-to-dockerfile>.dockerignore`, which BuildKit honours where it is
#      supported:
#
#        for f in containers/*.Dockerfile; do cp containers/.dockerignore "$f.dockerignore"; done
#
# Neither exists in this repository right now.
#
# VERIFICATION STATUS: never exercised. Docker is not installed on the
# authoring host.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies. Reinstalled inside the builder stage with `npm ci` from the
# lockfile. Copying a host node_modules in would be slow, would break on a
# platform mismatch (macOS arm64 host, linux container), and would bypass the
# lockfile entirely.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output. Recompiled in the builder stage. A stale host `dist/` copied
# into the context is the classic way to ship code that does not match the
# source it was supposedly built from.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
**/dist/
build/
**/build/
.vite/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local runtime state: context database, audit log, sandbox scratch. Never
# belongs in an image. This is real user data.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
var/
**/var/
.sairios/
sandbox/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VM artifacts. Multi-gigabyte disk images for the QEMU path, which is the
# other half of the Docker/QEMU split and has nothing to do with these images.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
vm/out/
vm/.cache/
*.qcow2
*.img
*.iso
*.raw

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Version control metadata. Large, and carries full history including anything
# that was ever committed and later removed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. `.env` holds provider credentials on some developers' machines.
# Nothing in this project needs a credential inside a container: agent-bridge
# runs in mock mode there. Listed so a secret cannot reach an image layer even
# by accident, which only becomes true once this list is in force. See the
# header: it is not in force today.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
openclaw/config/local/
openclaw/workspace/.credentials*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test and coverage output.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
coverage/
**/coverage/
.vitest/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend sources. The three service images are backend only; the shell is
# served by Vite on the host during development. Excluding this keeps unrelated
# UI edits from busting the service build cache.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
apps/shell/src/
apps/shell/public/
apps/shell/index.html
apps/shell/vite.config.ts

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation and tooling that no image needs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/
containers/
*.md
!README.md
.editorconfig
.prettierrc.json
.prettierignore
eslint.config.js
vitest.config.ts

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS and editor noise.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
